  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information involves the low-probability outcomes in both lotteries, specifically those with probabilities below 20%. In this case, both lotteries have outcomes below this threshold: Lottery A has a 0.2% chance of -3000 Euros, and Lottery B has a 0.1% chance of -6000 Euros. According to the decision reason, these probabilities are to be weighted by increasing them by 10 percentage points (i.e., 0.2% becomes 10.2%, and 0.1% becomes 10.1%). The weighted outcomes are then compared: for Lottery A, the weighted disutility is (-3000) * (0.102) = -306; for Lottery B, it is (-6000) * (0.101) = -606. The decision reason would prefer Lottery A, as it has the less negative (more favorable) weighted outcome.",
