  "step_3": "The decision reason requires a specific reweighting of low-probability events (below 20%) by increasing their probability by 10 percentage points and then evaluating the expected value under this transformation. While the individual does consider the low-probability outcomes (which aligns with the scope of the reason), there is no evidence that they adjusted the probabilities in the prescribed way or performed any calculation resembling the weighted sum. The justification is based on the unattractiveness of the -6000 outcome, which suggests a focus on outcome severity rather than a rule-based comparison of reweighted expected values. Therefore, although the individual attends to the same outcomes that the decision reason highlights, they do not appear to use the specific rule or calculation method defined by the reason. The deliberation is more consistent with a qualitative aversion to large losses than with a formal reweighting procedure.",
